cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Safe MarketUniverses: Can Model-Emitted Uncertainty Ration Scarce Oversight Under Corrupted Evidence?"
message: "If you use Safe MarketUniverses, please cite this software artifact."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Zavala"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    affiliation: "Carnegie Mellon University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pazare/safe-market-universes"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-11"
abstract: "Safe MarketUniverses measures whether model-emitted uncertainty signals can allocate a scarce human-review budget under corrupted evidence, scored as regret against an oracle that spends the same budget optimally from hindsight utilities the model never sees."
license: MIT
